      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For example, suppose I want to create a vignette or dimming effect. If I use a full-screen overlay, the Translucent Personal Mirror will pierce through the effect. To fix this, I can apply the shader inside the mirror's rendering pass as well. However, this causes the effect to run on regular world mirrors too, resulting in the effect overlapping with the first-person view (or camera view) and being applied twice inside the world mirror.\n\nFurthermore, inside the handheld camera view, the Translucent Personal Mirror is processed the exact same way as a regular mirror. This means that when looking through the camera (with UI visibility turned on), the effect overlaps on the Translucent Personal Mirror as well, creating a visual mismatch compared to how it looks in the normal first-person view.\n\nThese issues could be cleanly resolved if we had the parameter requested in this Canny to detect whether it is a Translucent Personal Mirror. With it, we would be able to conditionally apply the effect inside the mirror's rendering pass only when viewed in the first-person view and when dealing with a Translucent Personal Mirror.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
