  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hello,\n\nI would like to request the addition of a new global shader parameter to detect the VRChat Personal Mirror.\n\nWhile creating custom shaders, I have encountered various issues (such as rendering queue mismatches) specifically when the shader is executed during the rendering pass of the \"Translucent\" Personal Mirror.\n\nTo solve these issues cleanly and efficiently, it would be extremely helpful to have global shader parameters that allow us to detect whether the current rendering pass belongs to a Personal Mirror, and whether it is opaque or translucent.\n\nSpecifically, I would love to see it implemented in a format similar to the following:\n\n[_VRChatPersonalMirrorMode]\n\n0 — Rendering normally, not in a mirror\n\n1 — Rendering inside an Opaque Personal Mirror\n\n2 — Rendering inside a Translucent Personal Mirror\n\nThis feature would significantly improve the flexibility and quality of custom shaders in VRChat. Thank you for your consideration!",
